    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "All 62 tests pass \u2014 **BUILD SUCCESS**, including the new `Cp50Tests` idempotency test.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented idempotent owner creation in `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner` (the handler for `POST /api/owners`).\n\nBecause `addOwner` implements the generated `OwnersApi` interface, I couldn't add a `@RequestHeader` parameter to its signature. Instead:\n\n- **Reading the header** \u2014 a `currentIdempotencyKey()` helper pulls the `Idempotency-Key` header off the current request via `RequestContextHolder`, returning the trimmed value or `null` when absent/blank.\n- **Store** \u2014 a `ConcurrentHashMap<String,Integer>` (`idempotentCreates`) on the singleton controller maps each seen key to the id of the owner its first successful create produced.\n- **Repeat handling** \u2014 at the top of `addOwner`, if the key is already in the store and that owner still exists, the original owner is returned with **200 OK** (via `ownerMapper.toOwnerDto`), short-circuiting before any validation/duplicate rules run \u2014 so no duplicate is created and it won't 409.\n- **Recording** \u2014 the key\u2192id entry is stored only after a create actually succeeds (`saveOwner`), so failed creates (400/409/429) don't burn the key.\n\nThe key is recorded only on success and the store is checked before the duplicate/quota rules, so a repeat returns 200 with the same id rather than the 409 those rules would otherwise produce \u2014 exactly what `Cp50Tests.coreIdempotentRepeat` asserts (`id1 == id2`, second call `isOk()`). All other 61 checkpoints remain green since the new logic is inert when no `Idempotency-Key` header is present.",
