    "probe_text": "Here is the complete, ordered sequence for `POST /api/owners`, which is handled by `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner(OwnerFieldsDto)` (`src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java:182`). I'll split it into what happens *before* the method body (framework-level) and then each step *inside* it, in source order.\n\n## Phase 0 \u2014 Before the method runs (framework)\n\n1. **Authorization** \u2014 `@PreAuthorize(\"hasRole(@roles.OWNER_ADMIN)\")`. Caller must hold the `OWNER_ADMIN` role, else the method is never entered.\n2. **Bean Validation on the request body** (`OwnerFieldsDto`), applied by Spring MVC before the handler:\n   - `firstName` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..30)`, `@Pattern(^[\\p{L}]+([ '-][\\p{L}]+){0,2}$)`\n   - `lastName` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..30)`, `@Pattern(...\\.?$)`\n   - `city` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..80)`, `@Pattern` (must contain a non-space char)\n   - `telephone` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..20)`, `@Pattern(^[0-9 ()+.-]*$)`\n   - `title` \u2014 `@Size(max 10)` (optional)\n   - `address` \u2014 `@Size(1..255)`, `@Pattern` non-blank (optional)\n   - `addressLine1` / `addressLine2` \u2014 `@Size(max 255)` (optional)\n   - `email` \u2014 `@Size(1..255)` (optional)\n   - `postcode` \u2014 `@Pattern(^[0-9]{4}$)` (optional; enforces the 4-digit syntax)\n\n## Phase 1 \u2014 Inside `addOwner`, in order\n\n3. **Idempotency short-circuit** \u2014 read the `Idempotency-Key` header. If it was seen before *and* the owner it created still exists, return that original owner with **200 OK** (no new owner, no further steps).\n4. **Map DTO \u2192 `Owner`** entity (`ownerMapper.toOwner`).\n5. **Future-date validation** \u2014 if a `registrationDate` was supplied and it is after today \u2192 **400 Bad Request**.\n6. **Registration-date normalization (side-effect)** \u2014 effective date = supplied date or today; roll it forward off weekends and the fixed public holidays via `toBusinessDay`; `owner.setRegistrationDate(...)`.\n7. **Daily-cap validation** \u2014 count existing owners already registered on that (adjusted) date; if `>= 100` \u2192 **429 Too Many Requests**.\n8. **Bulk-signup flag (side-effect)** \u2014 `owner.setBulkSignupWarning(createdToday > 80)`.\n9. **Address application/normalization** (`applyAddress`, side-effect + validation) \u2014 prefer `addressLine1` (normalize: trim, collapse whitespace, upper-case, expand ST/RD/AVE; compose flat `address` from line1 + line2), otherwise normalize the flat `address`. If neither a usable `addressLine1` nor `address` is present \u2192 **400 Bad Request**.\n10. **Telephone normalization/validation (side-effect)** \u2014 `toE164` strips separators, assumes `+61` when no country code, enforces 8\u201315 total digits and the per-country national-number length (`+61`\u21929, `+1`\u219210). If it can't form a valid E.164 number \u2192 **400**. Otherwise `owner.setTelephone(e164)`.\n11. **Email normalization/validation (side-effect, only if email present)** \u2014 `normalizeEmail` (trim + lower-case); if it fails `EMAIL_PATTERN` \u2192 **400**; if its domain is a disposable domain (`mailinator.com`, `tempmail.com`, `guerrillamail.com`) \u2192 **400**; else `owner.setEmail(normalized)`.\n12. **Postcode-vs-region validation** \u2014 derive region from city (`CITY_REGION`) and check the postcode is within that region's range (NSW 2000\u20132099, VIC 3000\u20133099, QLD 4000\u20134099; unknown region accepts any). If out of range \u2192 **400**.\n13. **City-size cap validation** \u2014 count existing owners in the same (normalized) city; if `>= 50` \u2192 **409 Conflict**.\n14. **Household id (side-effect)** \u2014 compute `householdId` = first 12 hex of SHA-256 of `normalizedLastName|postcode`; `owner.setHouseholdId(...)`.\n15. **Household size (side-effect)** \u2014 gather non-deleted members with the same `householdId`; `owner.setHouseholdSize(members + 1)`.\n16. **Household-duplicate validation** \u2014 if the household already has members *and* `sharesHousehold` is not true \u2192 **409 Conflict**.\n17. **Identity-key duplicate validation** \u2014 build `identityKey` = `telephone|email|householdId`; if any non-deleted owner already has the same key \u2192 **409 Conflict**.\n18. **Possible-duplicate flag (side-effect)** \u2014 if `sharesHousehold` is true, set `possibleDuplicate = false`; otherwise find the lowest-id non-deleted owner with the same normalized last name + same postcode + a *different* telephone, and if found set `possibleDuplicate = true` and `possibleDuplicateOf = that id`, else `possibleDuplicate = false`.\n19. **Customer code (side-effect)** \u2014 `customerCode` = `<REGION>-<HASH8>` (region from locality, HASH8 = SHA-256 of telephone+lastName), appending `-<n>` (n\u22652) to resolve collisions with existing codes; `owner.setCustomerCode(...)`.\n20. **Namesake count (side-effect)** \u2014 count owners with the same normalized first *and* last name; `owner.setNamesakeCount(...)`.\n21. **Persist (side-effect)** \u2014 `clinicService.saveOwner(owner)`. At persistence, the `Owner` entity's own Bean Validation runs: `address` `@NotEmpty`, `city` `@NotEmpty`, `telephone` `@NotEmpty` + `@Pattern(^\\+[0-9]{8,15}$)`.\n22. **Record idempotency key (side-effect)** \u2014 if a key was supplied, store `key \u2192 owner.id` in `idempotentCreates`.\n23. **Audit log (side-effect)** \u2014 `AUDIT.info(...)` records id, customerCode, registrationDate, membershipLevel, membershipNumber.\n24. **Respond** \u2014 map to `OwnerDto`, set `Location: /api/owners/{id}`, return **201 Created**.\n\nA couple of notes worth flagging:\n- Several \"derived\" attributes on the response (e.g. `salutation`, `ageBand`, `membershipLevel`/`membershipPoints`, `fiscalYear`, `checkDigit`, `timezone`, `locality`, `telephoneDisplay`) are **computed on read** by getters in `Owner`, not set during creation \u2014 so they aren't create-time side-effects, though the audit line and the returned DTO do read some of them.\n- The persisted `registrationDate`, `telephone`, `address`, and `email` are the *normalized* values, not the raw inputs."
